Licence for derived data files
==============================

Two files in this repository have different answers, and one licence statement
cannot cover both. They are treated separately below.

The source code is licensed separately under the MIT License (see LICENSE).
Cite as described in CITATION.cff.


1. The frozen assay matrix — CC BY 4.0, without qualification
-------------------------------------------------------------

`data/frozen/frozen-matrix-v1.parquet` contains the saturation genome editing
measurements and their coordinates, region classes and oriented functional
scores. It contains NO predictor score column.

It is released under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence
(CC BY 4.0): https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Upstream terms that continue to apply:

    Gene     MaveDB URN                    Upstream licence
    -------  ----------------------------  ----------------
    BRCA1    urn:mavedb:00000097-0-2       CC0 1.0
    BRCA2    urn:mavedb:00001225-a-1       CC0 1.0
    BARD1    urn:mavedb:00001250-a-2       CC0 1.0
    PALB2    urn:mavedb:00001259-a-2       CC0 1.0
    BAP1     urn:mavedb:00000662-0-1       CC BY 4.0
    RAD51C   urn:mavedb:00000673-0-1       CC BY 4.0
    VHL      urn:mavedb:00000675-a-1       CC BY 4.0

  The three CC BY 4.0 deposits require attribution to their originating
  publications, which are cited in the manuscript and in CITATION.cff. Of these
  SEVEN DEPOSIT LICENCES, CC BY 4.0 is the most restrictive, so the CC BY 4.0
  release of this file is compatible with all seven. That reasoning is about the
  seven MaveDB deposits only; it does not extend to section 2.


2. The score matrices and everything derived from them — mixed terms
---------------------------------------------------------------------

`results/score_matrix_atlas_v*.parquet`, every table under `results/`, and every
figure and table in the manuscript that is computed from them carry nineteen
third-party predictor columns whose terms differ column by column. The CC BY 4.0
grant above does NOT lift them, and no single licence describes this file.

  PER-COLUMN LICENCE TERMS ARE IN `results/predictor_resources_v1.tsv`
  (columns `licence` and `licence_source`), which is the single source of
  truth. `results/` is generated, not tracked in git: the table ships in the
  archived release, and in a git checkout it appears once
  `python -m atlas.predictor_resources` has been run. The summary below is
  therefore complete on its own, so that this file stands without it.

Summary as of the 2026-08-28 audit:

  * EIGHT columns are more restrictive than CC BY 4.0. Each restriction travels
    with its column and with any figure or table derived from it:

      alphagenome             non-commercial (API free tier)
      cadd                    non-commercial; commercial licence from UW
      alphamissense           CC BY-NC-SA 4.0
      nucleotide_transformer  CC BY-NC-SA 4.0
      spliceai_ds             CC BY-NC 4.0 (trained models, Illumina)
      revel                   non-commercial
      primateai               CC BY-NC 4.0 (trained models, Illumina)
      vest4                   non-commercial; excluded from dbNSFP's
                              commercial branch

    Two of these -- alphamissense and nucleotide_transformer -- are ShareAlike
    as well as NonCommercial.

  * EIGHT columns carry no restriction beyond attribution: gpn_msa (MIT),
    evo2 (Apache-2.0), phylop100way and phastcons100way (UCSC track data, free
    for commercial use), esm1b (MIT), pangolin_score (see below), and
    gnomad_af_global and gnomad_af_popmax (CC0 1.0).

  * THREE columns have NO LICENCE TERMS THAT COULD BE LOCATED:
    bayesdel_addaf, clinpred and metarnn. Each is supplied through the dbNSFP
    academic branch. An absent licence statement is not a permissive one and
    must not be read as one; a reuser needing certainty should contact those
    authors or drop the three columns.

  Pangolin. `pangolin_score` was produced by running Pangolin, which is licensed
  GPL-3.0. Running a GPL-licensed program does not place its output under the
  GPL, so the column is recorded as unencumbered by that licence. This is a
  stated decision rather than an omission.

  dbNSFP. The seven meta-predictor columns (revel, bayesdel_addaf, clinpred,
  metarnn, primateai, vest4, esm1b) are read from dbNSFP through the
  MyVariant.info batch API. dbNSFP ships an academic branch and a commercial
  branch with restricted components removed; because the requested fields
  include PrimateAI, VEST4 and REVEL, these values come from the ACADEMIC
  branch. MyVariant.info's terms add no permission of their own -- they disclaim
  warranties and pass upstream obligations through to the user.

Because the restricted columns cover between 40.2% and 100% of the matrix, a
reuser whose purpose is commercial can drop those eight columns and retain a
usable matrix. That is why the terms are declared per column rather than as a
blanket restriction on the whole file.


Reference genome and annotation
-------------------------------

GRCh38 sequence and Ensembl annotation under `data/refs/` are redistributed
under the terms of their providers (Ensembl: no restriction; UCSC track data:
free for public and commercial use). These files are not included in the Zenodo
archive; `make fetch` retrieves them from source.
